The Duchess is a 2008 historical drama film directed by Saul Dibb, who co-wrote the screenplay with Jeffrey Hatcher and Anders Thomas Jensen, based on the 1998
book Georgiana, Duchess of Devonshire by Amanda Foreman, about the late 18th-century English aristocrat Georgiana Cavendish, Duchess of Devonshire.

11
01:07:13,333 --> 01:07:19,333
She was a distant relation of Diana, Princess of Wales, where the quote "There were
three people in her marriage" in the promotional poster comes from.

12
01:13:20,000 --> 01:13:26,000
The Duchess was the older sister of Lady Diana's
great-great-great-grandfather, George Spencer, 2nd Earl Spencer.

13
01:19:26,666 --> 01:19:32,666
The Duchess was released on 5 September 2008 in the United Kingdom.

14
